Draft date: November 2026
Notes:
	Sample script for testing Slugline.
	It covers the Fountain features the parser supports.

# ACT ONE

= Ruth and Eli ride into a town that doesn't want them.

EXT. DESERT ROAD - DAWN #1#

The sun cracks the horizon. Two riders, RUTH (40s, weathered) and ELI (17, nervous), move slowly through the heat.

ELI
How far now?

RUTH
(not looking at him)
Far enough that you stop asking.

[[Maybe add a shot of the vultures here.]]

EXT. SILVER CREEK - MAIN STREET - DAY #2#

A dusty street. Shutters close as the riders pass.

ELI (V.O.)
Ma always said the quiet towns were the worst ones.

Ruth stops her horse in front of the SALOON.

RUTH
Stay with the horses.

ELI
But—

RUTH (CONT'D)
Stay.

CUT TO:

INT. SALOON - CONTINUOUS #3#

Dim. A piano nobody plays. Behind the bar, the SHERIFF (60s) dries a glass that is already dry.

SHERIFF
We don't serve your kind here.

RUTH
You don't know my kind.

SHERIFF ^
Everybody knows your kind.

/* Cut line:
RUTH
Then you know why I came.
*/

Ruth lays a tin badge on the bar.

.FLASHBACK - THE RANCH FIRE #3A#

Flames. A younger Ruth carries a child out of a burning barn.

INT./EXT. RUTH'S WAGON - NIGHT #4#

Eli counts bullets by lamplight.

@McCALLISTER (O.S.)
I'd count them twice, son.

Eli freezes.

EXT. SILVER CREEK - MAIN STREET - NIGHT #5#

!THE STREET IS EMPTY.

Ruth walks to the middle of the street and waits.

> FADE OUT.

>THE END<
